# Room Flow frontend stack

Do not change this stack. Do not suggest other frontend frameworks unless explicitly asked.

## Front-end

- Angular, TypeScript, JavaScript
- RxJS, NgRx, Signals
- Angular Material, HTML5, CSS3, SCSS
- Performance: lazy loading, standalone components, ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush

## Conventions

- Standalone components only (no NgModules)
- Every component uses `changeDetection: ChangeDetectionStrategy.OnPush` (not inherited from the parent; Default is Angular’s default)
- Feature routes under `frontend/src/app/features`, lazy-loaded with `loadComponent`
- HTTP via Angular `HttpClient`; talk to the API through `/api` (dev proxy in `proxy.conf.json`)
- Prefer Signals for component state; use RxJS for HTTP and streams; use NgRx when state is shared across features. Do not mutate arrays/objects in place when they are read by the template — replace via `signal.set` / `update`
- Style with Angular Material and BEM/SCSS; keep a consistent Design System (do not invent a parallel UI kit, do not use Tailwind)
- Custom component CSS uses BEM: `block__element--modifier` (e.g. `rooms__status--error`). Do not style via tag descendants (`.rooms h1`); give the element its own class. Nest SCSS as `&__element` / `&--modifier` under the block.
- Colors and fonts live in `frontend/src/styles/_variables.scss` as SCSS variables. Import with `@use 'variables' as tokens` and use `tokens.$color-text` — do not hardcode hex values in components.
